# Two RUN -> STBY -> RUN excursions of GPC2, ten seconds apart (#173, #175).
#
# One excursion, traced, is modelled correctly: GPC2 puts up sync 000 ~1.2 s
# after the switch (the software poll), GPC1 reads it at once and removes it
# from the set cleanly, and on RUN it goes 000 -> 111, which FCMCSYNC readmits
# on.  No vote.  But the votes seen by hand arrived on the SECOND excursion,
# so this does two -- and times them, because by hand the spacing varied and a
# short excursion fell inside the poll and did nothing at all.
#
# Waits for both talkbacks first, so GPC2 is an established member of the set
# when it is taken out (the condition #176 used to make unreachable).
#
# A `wait` takes no time prefix; every other line needs one.
+0     gpc 2
wait gpc 2 mode-tb RUN timeout 300
+0     gpc 1
wait gpc 1 mode-tb RUN timeout 300
+5     gpc 2
+0     mode STANDBY
+10    mode RUN
+10    mode STANDBY
+10    mode RUN
